# Local stack troubleshooting

Read `tmp/linux-stack/logs/` and run `bash dev/linux/dev.sh status` first.
For stale services, use `bash dev/linux/dev.sh stop` followed by `start`.
Use `reset` only when intentionally recreating local data. Never reset a hosted backend.

Port conflicts require identifying the existing listener with `ss -ltnp`; do not
kill unrelated processes or switch ports silently. Confirm native `docker info`
works in the Linux user session. Docker Desktop and Windows port repair are obsolete.

Type generation must preserve the existing file on a CLI error or missing anchors.
Use `.cursor/hooks/workflow.sh sync-types` with a migration edit payload.
For map rendering, follow `fleet-map.mdc` and check the browser's CSP diagnostics.
Require healthy app, docs, Auth, and database-backed Edge probes before claiming a fix.
